From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shirogane <artoriapendragon123@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] ASoC: sun4i-codec: add the D1/T113 audio codec

The D1 carries the same codec as the T113, and neither is supported
upstream: sun4i-codec's match table stops at H616 and F1C100s, and
sound/soc/sunxi has no analog half for this generation at all.

Two pieces are needed. sun4i-codec gets a sun20i-d1 quirks entry -- its
own regmap layout, its own ADC/DAC FIFO control fields, and a card whose
routes wire the ADCs and DACs to the analog component named by
allwinner,codec-analog-controls. The clocks are the second difference
worth calling out: this codec has separate ADC and DAC module clocks
rather than the single "codec" clock every earlier part uses, which is
what has_dual_clock selects.

The analog half is a new driver rather than a quirks entry in
sun8i-codec-analog, because on this SoC it is plain MMIO at 0x02030300
instead of the ADDA-PR indirect register bus. sun8i-codec-analog is left
alone: a match there would claim the same compatible and bind by link
order.

Ported from the T113 tree (Shirogane Tsumugi's 6.18 branch), minus its
change to the H616 quirks -- upstream marks that part playback_only, so
the ADC fields it added there are dead weight at best.

Playback is what has been exercised. The capture path comes over as it
was written, and its own commit message there calls it incomplete.
---
